# The platform's central guarantee is a SHA-256 over canonical bytes. `core.autocrlf` is on for the
# Windows checkout this repository is developed in, which means without this file the bytes on disk
# depend on the operating system. Nothing tracked today is hashed raw — `ContentHash::of_bytes` is
# fed by ingested source files, and no CSV or TSV fixture is committed yet — so this is prevention,
# not a fix for an observed break.
#
# It is worth the file anyway. A CRLF/LF digest mismatch is a bug that reproduces on one machine and
# not another, and it has already cost a sibling project a ledger that verified 0 of 24 entries.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Certificates, golden fixtures, schemas and the CPython reference all participate in cross-language
# parity. Their bytes are not allowed to depend on the checkout.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or the shebang line carries a carriage return and Linux CI reports a
# missing interpreter.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Data formats that reach ContentHash::of_bytes. There is no such file tracked yet; the rule exists
# so that adding one does not silently make its digest platform-dependent.
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf

Cargo.lock text eol=lf
